  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 1.4. Strengthened social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Tripartite labour advisory council established in Lumbini Provinces in February 2020.
 1. Nepal&apos;s Labour Act  2017 makes provision for the establishment of tripartite social dialogue mechanisms at a province level. This is in line with the government&apos;s efforts to create a federalized governance structure in the country. The ILO provided extensive technical support to pilot the establishment of a tripartite social dialogue council in one province, namely Lumbini Province (formerly Province 5).  The ILO&apos;s support included the drafting of a Constitution for the mechanism, as well as tripartite training workshops on tripartite social dialogue. The Lumbini Province tripartite structure provides a model for the establishment of similar structures in other provinces. It was launched in February 2020, and is currently engaging on the development of a Labour and Employment Policy for the province.</narrative>
   </description>
